  "topic": "arrays-hashing",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "pattern": "arrays-hashing / Dutch flag",
  "statement": "# Sort Colors\n\nGiven an array `nums` containing `n` elements colored red, white, or blue (represented as `0`, `1`, and `2` respectively), sort them in-place so that objects of the same color are adjacent, in the order `0`, `1`, and `2`.\n\nReturn the sorted array.\n\nConstraints: `1 <= nums.length <= 100` and `0 <= nums[i] <= 2`.\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "nums = [0]",
      "output": "[0]",
      "explanation": "A single-element array [0] is already sorted: the output is [0]."
    },
    {
      "input": "nums = [2, 1, 0]",
      "output": "[0, 1, 2]",
      "explanation": "The input [2, 1, 0] is the reverse of the target order; the three-way partition swaps 2 to the right, 0 to the left, and leaves 1 in the middle, producing [0, 1, 2]."
    }
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "Function signature: `function sortColors(nums: number[])`.",
    "Inputs are JSON-serializable values satisfying the bounds stated above."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Can you partition the array into three contiguous regions (0s, 1s, 2s) in a single pass without sorting?",
    "The Dutch National Flag uses three pointers: everything before 'low' is 0, everything after 'high' is 2, and 'mid' scans the unknown middle region.",
    "Initialize low=0, mid=0, high=n-1. When arr[mid]==0, swap with low (++low, ++mid). When arr[mid]==2, swap with high (--high). When arr[mid]==1, ++mid."
  ],
